  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "transparent": true,
      "options": {
        "mode": "html",
        "content": "<div style=\"padding:2px 8px;opacity:.85\">\n<b>One front door for every signal:</b> the OpenTelemetry Collector pulls forest data (prometheus receiver → json-exporter), probes the APIs (http_check), tails container logs (file_log) and receives traces from Grafana, Prometheus and Alertmanager (OTLP).\nIt pushes metrics to Prometheus <i>natively over OTLP</i>, traces to Tempo (tail-sampled) and logs to Loki (OTLP). Prometheus scrapes the collector's own health directly — the meta-monitoring does not depend on the pipeline it watches.</div>",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
